**CShareTechnologyAction slot 7** - one holder (vftable 0x15FBCD4), 0xCA bytes, 0xA4B780 to the two bare `ret`s at 0xA4B818 and 0xA4B849 (one body: the second is the `value == 0` arm, jumped to from 0xA4B791), 6 int3 before CShareTechnologyAction slot 11. **The whole family's shape in 42 instructions, which is why it is the one to read first.** `this` in ECX, no stack arguments.

    if (!this->value) { 0x507C10(GetCountry(recipient)@stack, GetCountry(actor)@ECX); return; }
    if (!this->+0x28) return;                        // the technology object
    countries[actor_id]->diplo_influence -= GetDefines()->diplomacy->SHARE_TECH_INFLUENCE_COST;
    if (that went below 0) it is set to 0;
    0x507B40(GetCountry(actor)@stack, this->+0x28->+0x5C@stack, GetCountry(recipient)@EAX);

It is the only member of the family that raises no message and touches no CDiplomacyStatus. `this->+0x28` is the shared technology (unnamed); its `+0x5C` is what 0x507B40 is given. 0x507B40 and 0x507C10 are a matched add/remove pair over a 0xC-byte-strided vector at `CCountry +0x6F0`, which is where the shared technology is recorded - both are unnamed and are in `frontier`. The name `Apply` is ours; the body is read end to end.

**The writer of `CDiplomacyStatus +0x38 relation`, which the record had as inferred with no writer identified.** 0x4E65C0 to the two `ret 4`s at 0x4E662B and 0x4E6635 - one body, two arms of the same clamp - 8 int3 before 0x4E6640. The receiver is in **EDI** and the other country's tag in **ECX**, with the delta the one stack argument, so it carries no ordinary calling convention and the annotations are explicit (trap 11).

    fwd = this->diplomacy[other->id];          // CCountry +0xE28
    fwd->changed (+0x59) = 1;
    v = clamp(delta + fwd->relation (+0x38), [0x1710C38], [0x1710C34]);
    fwd->relation = v;
    rev = other->GetCountry()->diplomacy[this->id];   // CCountryTag::GetCountry, 0x402610
    rev->changed = 1;
    rev->relation = v;

So **relation is symmetric by construction** - the same clamped value is written to both directions, and the delta is applied to the forward side's current value only. The two clamp globals are `[0x1710C34] = 200000` and `[0x1710C38] = -200000`, i.e. **relation is thousandths on a -200.000..+200.000 scale** (trap 7), which is the range the game's own diplomacy screen shows. Eighteen call sites, all inside the family's slot 7, each passing one of the `*_RELATION_CHANGE` defines - and those defines are stored x1000, so the units match end to end.
